Hi folks,
The OSFRTDEV subset is no more needed for ORACLE RDBMS with DU 4.0b. It has 
been included in OSFLIBAxxx (OSFLIBA410 - libm.a library )

Thanks to :

Olle Eriksson olle@cb.uu.se

OSFRTDEV350 is for some version of Digital Unix 3.2A/B/C/D/E/F/G. The Real 
time stiff in the basic subsets in 4.0A/B/C/D and the realtime subsets have 
been retired.
------------------------------------------------------------------------  
------

Julian Rodriguez Julian.Rodriguez@digital.com

Jacques,

this subset is no longer shipped separately, but it's included within the 
base operating system. The Oracle documentation is obsolete.



------------------------------------------------------------------------  
------
jmh@zk3.dec.com (Jan Mark Holzer, UEG) :

Hi,

as of Digital-UNIX V4.0B the RT libraries have been moved to the BaseOS 
subsets (OSFBASE4xx) .  It seems ORACLE for some reason is checking for the 
existence of the OSFRTDEV subsets. You can " fake " these subsets by simply 
creating to empty files called OSFDEVRT425.lk and OSFDEVRT425.ctrl (you can 
use touch to creat them), this will make ORACLE believe the subsets are 
installed.
ORACLE is mots likely trying to use librt which now can be found in 
OSFBASE425.inv and should reside in /usr/ccs/lib/librt.a .
Hth,
Jan
------------------------------------------------------------------------  
------

"Dr. Ram Rao" ram@ini.dec.com

This subset is only needed when installing Oracle on V3.2x.  It can be 
safely ignored while installing on V4.0x.  (All the functionality in this 
optional subset has been moved into a mandatory subset in V4.0x)
Ram

and ORACLE Corporate Support on the WEB

