conclude that this is a wise thing to do. However, there was no consensus=
 on
how often defragmenting should be done; some did it weekly/monthly, other=
s
daily and others used a mixed scheme. The mixed scheme consisted of cron
runs and manual defrags if the cron run did not defrag "good enough" (the=

majority of those who ran that mixed scheme had a personal feeling on wha=
t
was considered to be "good enough"). The rule of thumb seems to be "defra=
g
more often if the filesystem is active, e.g news/mail/print spools etc."

