To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: fcntl: Local Lock-manager...
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078708811623


  
  	this message indicates  a NFS client tried to use NFS
  	locking for file access and it hasn't been enabled on
  	your system, or the lock-manager is no longer registered
  	with the portmapper (you can check for the lock-manager 
  	using the command "#rpcinfo -p <SystemName>|grep lock". 
  	You can enable NFS locking by setting the NFSLOCKING 
  	variabel to "1" in /etc/rc.config (either use nfssetup or 
  	"#rcmgr set NFSLOCKING 1" .

Yes, that did take care of it.  There were no statd nor lockd 
processes running.  After doing the rcmgr, started them by
hand, and the portmapper showed them after that.

Didn't find the source file, we don't appear to have them.

