=0A=
=0A=
--with-stabs option of configure:=0A=
=0A=
	On MIPS based systems and on Alphas, you must specify whether=0A=
	you want GNU CC to create the normal ECOFF debugging format,=0A=
	or to use BSD-style stabs passed through the ECOFF symbol=0A=
	table.  The normal ECOFF debug format cannot fully handle=0A=
	languages other than C.  BSD stabs format can handle other=0A=
	languages, but it only works with the GNU debugger GDB.=0A=
=0A=
	Normally, GNU CC uses the ECOFF debugging format by default;=0A=
	if you prefer BSD stabs, specify `--with-stabs' when you=0A=
	configure GNU CC.=0A=
=0A=
	No matter which default you choose when you configure GNU CC,=0A=
	the user can use the `-gcoff' and `-gstabs+' options to=0A=
	specify explicitly the debug format for a particular=0A=
	compilation.=0A=
=0A=
	`--with-stabs' is meaningful on the ISC system on the 386,=0A=
	also, if `--with-gas' is used.  It selects use of stabs=0A=
	debugging information embedded in COFF output.  This kind of=0A=
	debugging information supports C++ well; ordinary COFF=0A=
	debugging information does not.=0A=
=0A=
	`--with-stabs' is also meaningful on 386 systems running=0A=
	SVR4.  It selects use of stabs debugging information embedded=0A=
