Thanks for the assist. Problem solved!

A couple of you suggested DNS involvement. I didn't check that when the problem
first occurred since /etc/svcorder is local then bind, and I *thought* that
would send me to /etc/hosts before using dns. The hosts file is OK.

Anyway, I checked /etc/resolv.conf and that was the problem. We changed 
our IP address a while back due to, well trust me, it would take too long
to explain.

Somehow this machine, which is a development platform, didn't get the 
name server address updated. I fixed that and all is well in ftp land
again.

Many thanks for the always speedy help from all of you.

-Burch-

