To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: Changing LEDs on an AS2100
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078708811874


The question was:

How does one change the LED on an AlphaServer 2100 at run time (that
is, while the operating system is running and not at the SRM console).

The answer is:

You don't.  Sort of.  There is a reference to the OCP in
/usr/sys/include/arch/alpha/iic.h under DU, but that appears to be for
something other than a 2100.  There may be a way, but it isn't
documented anywhere that I've been able to find.  The operator is
pretty much limited to using 'set ocp_text [msg]' at the SRM console
prompt.

